116
00:07:47.515 --> 00:07:51.559
You and I have walked out a lot of places
that no one should have walked out of.

117
00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:54.271
Yes. but this is Cary. okay.
He's not like us.

118
00:07:54.772 --> 00:07:56.689
- I still have to kill spiders for him.
- [chuckles]

119
00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:57.983
Drive faster. please.

120
00:07:58.818 --> 00:08:00.444
[engine revving]

121
00:08:02.613 --> 00:08:04.531
I know how this looks. okay?

122
00:08:04.532 --> 00:08:07.158
And part of the reason it looks that way
is because it is that way.

123
00:08:07.159 --> 00:08:08.576
I can't deny that.

124
00:08:08.577 --> 00:08:11.121
And I'm not gonna sit here
and try and excuse what I've done.

125
00:08:11.122 --> 00:08:13.916
But I've had some time to think about it.
and even now…

126
00:08:14.416 --> 00:08:16.626
even now. standing here with you.

127
00:08:16.627 --> 00:08:20.046
I don't know if I would have been able
to do things any differently. okay?

128
00:08:20.047 --> 00:08:22.382
And believe me. however much you hate me

129
00:08:22.383 --> 00:08:23.675
right now in this moment.

130
00:08:23.676 --> 00:08:26.970
it doesn't even… it doesn't fucking
compare to how much I hate myself for it.

131
00:08:26.971 --> 00:08:28.888
I think you might
be underestimating me. honey.

132
00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:31.391
- Don't say that.
- Well. I don't know who you are.

133
00:08:31.392 --> 00:08:33.143
- Yes. you do. You know me.
- Cary. no. I don't.

134
00:08:33.144 --> 00:08:34.602
The person I know wouldn't do this.

135
00:08:34.603 --> 00:08:36.563
You're the only person
who's ever known me. Lucky.

136
00:08:36.564 --> 00:08:37.565
Clearly.

137
00:08:40.234 --> 00:08:41.901
Look. I made a mistake.

138
00:08:41.902 --> 00:08:43.154
I know I made a mistake.

139
00:08:43.779 --> 00:08:45.488
But you're not gonna stand there
and convince me

140
00:08:45.489 --> 00:08:47.407
that what we have isn't real. okay?

141
00:08:47.408 --> 00:08:50.034
I fell in love with you
two seconds after I saw you.

142
00:08:50.035 --> 00:08:52.370
- And asking you to marry me...
- Okay. so when did the lies start?

143
00:08:52.371 --> 00:08:53.872
- What?
- Well. was it before the wedding?

144
00:08:53.873 --> 00:08:55.582
- No. That was all real.
- After the wedding?

145
00:08:55.583 --> 00:08:58.209
I know it might be difficult
to pinpoint an exact date.

146
00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:01.045
but I'm just trying to get a general
picture of when my life became a lie...

147
00:09:01.046 --> 00:09:02.423
She was going to kill you!

148
00:09:03.758 --> 00:09:05.800
My darling boy.

149
00:09:05.801 --> 00:09:07.218
Hello. Mother.

150
00:09:07.219 --> 00:09:09.095
- Look at you.
- Hello.

151
00:09:09.096 --> 00:09:10.346
[chuckles]

152
00:09:10.347 --> 00:09:11.724
[Priscilla clicks tongue] Oh.

153
00:09:13.517 --> 00:09:15.060
Oh. I missed you.

154
00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:21.859
- [chuckles]
- [sighs]

155
00:09:22.401 --> 00:09:23.402
Come on.

156
00:09:25.362 --> 00:09:27.530
I would have visited you if you'd let me.

157
00:09:27.531 --> 00:09:29.866
Oh. I couldn't let you see me in there.

158
00:09:29.867 --> 00:09:30.993
[chuckles]

159
00:09:32.703 --> 00:09:35.331
Yeah. I just really hate
that you were in there and not Wayne.

160
00:09:35.915 --> 00:09:36.998
It's okay.

161
00:09:36.999 --> 00:09:38.416
It's not.

162
00:09:38.417 --> 00:09:40.628
[chuckles] Well. listen.

163
00:09:41.337 --> 00:09:45.424
All that matters is I am here now.

164
00:09:46.592 --> 00:09:48.511
[chuckles] Here. sit down.

165
00:09:54.934 --> 00:09:55.935
How did you get out?

166
00:09:56.685 --> 00:09:58.646
Uh. good behavior.

167
00:09:59.271 --> 00:10:00.523
Wayne's lawyers?

168
00:10:04.485 --> 00:10:05.820
What's in it for him?

169
00:10:07.196 --> 00:10:10.449
Well. it's been brought to my attention
that there's some money missing.

170
00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.708
Does that have something to do with me?

171
00:10:20.292 --> 00:10:23.169
Well. John's been stealing
from me for years.

172
00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:24.462
Skimming.

173
00:10:24.463 --> 00:10:27.006
And the only person
who knows where that money is.

174
00:10:27.007 --> 00:10:28.426
is that little girlfriend of yours.

175
00:10:30.553 --> 00:10:32.388
- Wife.
- What?

176
00:10:34.974 --> 00:10:36.183
You're married?

177
00:10:37.685 --> 00:10:38.893
You didn't tell me?

178
00:10:38.894 --> 00:10:40.229
You wouldn't see me.

179
00:10:41.272 --> 00:10:42.273
Listen.

180
00:10:43.607 --> 00:10:45.484
I know it's been hard. okay?

181
00:10:46.277 --> 00:10:48.361
You had to do what you had to do
to survive.

182
00:10:48.362 --> 00:10:49.779
But I'm out now.

183
00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:54.617
And we're gonna get our business in order
and everything is gonna go back to normal.

184
00:10:54.618 --> 00:10:56.536
I love her. Mom.

185
00:10:56.537 --> 00:10:58.788
Oh. come on. What happened to you?

186
00:10:58.789 --> 00:11:01.583
I'm gone for two years.
I-I don't even recognize you.

187
00:11:01.584 --> 00:11:04.169
Well. I'm happy. Maybe that's why
you don't recognize me.

188
00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:05.503
- Oh. you're not happy.
- I am.

189
00:11:05.504 --> 00:11:06.589
Look at you. You're bored.

190
00:11:07.673 --> 00:11:11.593
You're working minimum wage
and playing house with that little girl.

191
00:11:11.594 --> 00:11:13.721
You're capable of so much more.

192
00:11:15.806 --> 00:11:17.266
It's a nice life.

193
00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:18.933
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

194
00:11:18.934 --> 00:11:20.560
Is that what you want?

195
00:11:20.561 --> 00:11:21.604
A nice life?

196
00:11:22.188 --> 00:11:24.022
Man. you got a seat at the table.

197
00:11:24.023 --> 00:11:25.815
Wayne is ready to bring you into the fold.

198
00:11:25.816 --> 00:11:28.985
Wayne does not…
Wayne does not give a shit about me. okay?

199
00:11:28.986 --> 00:11:30.737
And he definitely does not
give a shit about you.

200
00:11:30.738 --> 00:11:33.573
Yeah. you bring in that money.
I promise you that's gonna change.

201
00:11:33.574 --> 00:11:35.492
I'm not doing this shit for Wayne. Mom.

202
00:11:35.493 --> 00:11:37.076
No. no. do it for yourself.

203
00:11:37.077 --> 00:11:39.954
I'm giving you a gift here.
This is a chance at a better life.

204
00:11:39.955 --> 00:11:41.164
What. like yours?

205
00:11:41.165 --> 00:11:42.708
You just got out of prison. Mom.

206
00:11:43.918 --> 00:11:45.001
Prison.

207
00:11:45.002 --> 00:11:48.172
I-I-I love that we're having
this conversation right now. I love it!

208
00:11:48.881 --> 00:11:51.008
Look. [sighs]

209
00:11:51.884 --> 00:11:54.302
Look. you could do it with the girl. okay?

210
00:11:54.303 --> 00:11:55.720
[scoffs]

211
00:11:55.721 --> 00:11:58.139
All you have to do is get her
to bring it to me.

212
00:11:58.140 --> 00:11:59.224
And then we're done.

213
00:11:59.225 --> 00:12:00.518
You can live your life.

214
00:12:01.102 --> 00:12:02.269
You know. you can…

215
00:12:02.812 --> 00:12:04.896
move to Fresno and work at Starbucks.

216
00:12:04.897 --> 00:12:07.233
I don't know. Whatever the fuck you want.

217
00:12:09.735 --> 00:12:10.985
So you're saying no?

218
00:12:10.986 --> 00:12:12.321
- I am.
- Okay. why?

219
00:12:12.905 --> 00:12:15.407
I'm in love. Mom.

220
00:12:16.367 --> 00:12:19.035
I'm in love. and I know
you wouldn't understand that.

221
00:12:19.036 --> 00:12:22.997
So you're sacrificing everything
for a girl who is lying to you?

222
00:12:22.998 --> 00:12:24.541
What are you talking about?

223
00:12:24.542 --> 00:12:26.835
That girl that
you're so madly in love with.

224
00:12:26.836 --> 00:12:29.712
You were busted by the fucking feds. Mom.

225
00:12:29.713 --> 00:12:31.590
Yeah. how do you think that happened?

226
00:12:34.802 --> 00:12:36.554
- Huh?
- No. Bullshit.

227
00:12:37.179 --> 00:12:40.056
That's bullshit. okay? Her father
went down in that bust. all right.

228
00:12:40.057 --> 00:12:42.475
So did she. right?
They took her away in cuffs. right?

229
00:12:42.476 --> 00:12:44.811
Yet she was never charged.
never even interrogated.

230
00:12:44.812 --> 00:12:47.730
No. no. no.
Because she was barely involved. Mom.

231
00:12:47.731 --> 00:12:51.025
She was an accessory. Cary.
With knowledge of the organization.

232
00:12:51.026 --> 00:12:52.193
And they let her walk.

233
00:12:52.194 --> 00:12:55.321
Did it never fucking occur to you
to ask her why?

234
00:12:55.322 --> 00:12:57.241
Are you really so fucking naive?

235
00:12:59.493 --> 00:13:00.828
Oh.

236
00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:10.587
Lucky knows where my money is
and you're gonna bring it to me.

237
00:13:10.588 --> 00:13:11.589
[Cary sighs]

238
00:13:13.257 --> 00:13:16.426
You know what Wayne's gonna do to me
if I don't bring him that money?

239
00:13:16.427 --> 00:13:18.345
Are you really gonna let that happen?

240
00:13:19.221 --> 00:13:20.805
Mom. [sighs]

241
00:13:20.806 --> 00:13:21.891
This is my life.

242
00:13:23.476 --> 00:13:25.644
There was a time
that meant something to you.

243
00:13:28.814 --> 00:13:30.900
You won't do it for me.
your fucking mother.

244
00:13:31.859 --> 00:13:35.153
Do it for your wife if you love her
the way you say you do.

245
00:13:35.154 --> 00:13:38.616
Because you know what happens to her
if I have to handle this myself.

246
00:13:47.291 --> 00:13:49.959
Okay? And you didn't think
to tell me any of this?

247
00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:53.046
[scoffs] Tell you? Tell you?

248
00:13:53.047 --> 00:13:55.590
- Are you fucking kidding me right now?
- Okay. Okay. We…

249
00:13:55.591 --> 00:13:58.051
- Don't turn it around right now.
- Don't turn it around?

250
00:13:58.052 --> 00:14:00.179
You worked with the feds
and you didn't tell me.

251
00:14:01.305 --> 00:14:03.223
You're the reason she went to prison.

252
00:14:03.224 --> 00:14:04.475
They were already on to her.

253
00:14:05.059 --> 00:14:07.435
- Bullshit.
- [stammers] I had no choice.

254
00:14:07.436 --> 00:14:09.395
When I said that two minutes ago.
you said. "Bullshit."

255
00:14:09.396 --> 00:14:11.065
Well. when you said it. it was.

256
00:14:14.652 --> 00:14:18.405
You can tell yourself whatever you want.
but you know I'm right.

257
00:14:18.989 --> 00:14:20.241
You lied to me.

258
00:14:22.493 --> 00:14:24.369
I wanted to tell you…

259
00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:25.995
- But you didn't. did you?
- But...

260
00:14:25.996 --> 00:14:28.706
You had years to tell me the truth.

261
00:14:28.707 --> 00:14:29.833
Years.

262
00:14:29.834 --> 00:14:32.460
The whole time we were married.
every time I talked to you about my mom.

263
00:14:32.461 --> 00:14:34.712
you never thought to mention
that you were the one who sold her out.

264
00:14:34.713 --> 00:14:36.423
- I-I couldn't.
- And now you come in here

265
00:14:36.424 --> 00:14:38.258
trying to claim some type
of moral high ground

266
00:14:38.259 --> 00:14:42.137
- telling me that I'm the one...
- Everything I did. I did for us. okay?

267
00:14:42.138 --> 00:14:43.888
I was trying to protect us.

268
00:14:43.889 --> 00:14:45.223
I was trying to protect you.

269
00:14:45.224 --> 00:14:47.559
Leaving me for dead in a hotel room
is not protecting me. Cary!

270
00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:50.019
I told you. if I didn't bring her
that money she was going to kill you.

271
00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:51.563
And she still will.

272
00:14:51.564 --> 00:14:55.191
What part of this
do you not understand. okay?

273
00:14:55.192 --> 00:14:58.904
She was. is. always will be bad news.

274
00:14:59.488 --> 00:15:01.156
You're just too close to see it.

275
00:15:01.157 --> 00:15:02.490
- She would not have stopped…
- Whoa.

276
00:15:02.491 --> 00:15:05.952
…until she got us all killed.
and I had to do something about it.

277
00:15:05.953 --> 00:15:07.120
I was too close?

278
00:15:07.121 --> 00:15:09.122
How the fuck is that any different
from you and John?

279
00:15:09.123 --> 00:15:10.623
Well. because my dad's not a gangster.

280
00:15:10.624 --> 00:15:12.417
Think you might be splitting hairs there.

281
00:15:12.418 --> 00:15:13.751
You know what?

282
00:15:13.752 --> 00:15:15.462
Do not talk about my father.

283
00:15:15.463 --> 00:15:18.131
Don't talk… Are you fucking kidding me?
Are you kidding me?

284
00:15:18.132 --> 00:15:19.466
This was all him.

285
00:15:19.467 --> 00:15:20.759
He did this.

286
00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:23.011
He fucked us
the moment he stole from Wayne.

287
00:15:23.012 --> 00:15:25.430
The whole reason
we're even in this position right now

288
00:15:25.431 --> 00:15:27.098
is because of him.

289
00:15:27.099 --> 00:15:28.100
It's him.

290
00:15:28.642 --> 00:15:30.811
And even now.
you're still too blind to see it.

291
00:15:32.855 --> 00:15:33.856
[sighs]

292
00:15:36.609 --> 00:15:39.652
[Rand] I need black and whites
at Ocean and Magnolia.

293
00:15:39.653 --> 00:15:42.071
a hundred yards from the house.
Do not engage.

294
00:15:42.072 --> 00:15:43.907
I repeat. do not engage.

295
00:15:43.908 --> 00:15:45.492
Don't let the suspects see the cars.

296
00:15:45.493 --> 00:15:46.576
Only intercept.

297
00:15:46.577 --> 00:15:49.497
Only intercept if he tries to flee.

298
00:15:50.956 --> 00:15:54.794
So there was never a cargo plane
to fly us out of Vegas. no Dominica.

299
00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:57.629
From the moment we decided
to take the money.

300
00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:59.715
you knew you were gonna take it from me.

301
00:16:05.846 --> 00:16:08.015
I knew the day before we left.
after I saw my mom.

302
00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.184
The night you couldn't sleep.

303
00:16:12.394 --> 00:16:13.521
<i>Figures.</i>

304
00:16:14.814 --> 00:16:15.940
So why didn't you…

305
00:16:17.233 --> 00:16:18.234
give her the money?

306
00:16:18.859 --> 00:16:19.902
I don't know.

307
00:16:21.487 --> 00:16:22.947
You don't know?

308
00:16:25.449 --> 00:16:27.076
[Cary] <i>I was trying to keep you safe.</i>

309
00:16:29.995 --> 00:16:31.372
It really is beautiful.

310
00:16:32.414 --> 00:16:33.958
[Cary] <i>I didn't want to betray you.</i>

311
00:16:37.211 --> 00:16:38.545
It really is.

312
00:16:38.546 --> 00:16:39.754
<i>Okay. I was torn.</i>

313
00:16:39.755 --> 00:16:41.215
To our old life.

314
00:16:41.841 --> 00:16:43.092
To our old life.

315
00:17:07.825 --> 00:17:09.201
[sighs]

316
00:17:15.415 --> 00:17:17.417
I mean. I'd just had
the worst night of my life.

317
00:17:17.418 --> 00:17:19.044
but I did what I was supposed to do.

318
00:17:19.545 --> 00:17:20.629
Um…

319
00:17:21.963 --> 00:17:24.090
<i>Made it there. drop with the money.</i>

320
00:17:24.091 --> 00:17:27.343
<i>It was at this roadside diner
off the highway and I was about to go in.</i>

321
00:17:27.344 --> 00:17:29.679
<i>trade cars. execute the plan.
she would have the money</i>

322
00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:31.181
and it would all be over.

323
00:17:31.182 --> 00:17:34.477
And I was watching her
through the window of this diner

324
00:17:35.102 --> 00:17:36.686
<i>having coffee with Dutch.</i>

325
00:17:36.687 --> 00:17:39.397
calmly waiting for me
to deliver the money to her feet.

326
00:17:39.398 --> 00:17:42.233
knowing without a doubt that I would do it
because she's her and I'm me.

327
00:17:42.234 --> 00:17:44.487
and that's how it's been
my whole goddamn life.

328
00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:49.241
And I'm…

329
00:17:49.784 --> 00:17:54.288
I'm sitting in my car
and I can see her face from where I'm at.

330
00:17:55.247 --> 00:17:56.331
<i>And she…</i>

331
00:17:56.332 --> 00:17:57.916
<i>she laughs.</i>

332
00:17:57.917 --> 00:17:59.919
[no audible dialogue]

333
00:18:09.595 --> 00:18:12.430
No idea what she was laughing at.
but it didn't matter. It didn't matter.

334
00:18:12.431 --> 00:18:15.600
She'd just destroyed the one thing
in my life that I loved.

335
00:18:15.601 --> 00:18:17.560
and she was sitting there laughing.

336
00:18:17.561 --> 00:18:19.563
[no audible dialogue]

337
00:18:21.273 --> 00:18:22.900
And something in me. just. it…

338
00:18:24.777 --> 00:18:26.653
<i>I wasn't gonna be
her fucking pawn anymore.</i>

339
00:18:26.654 --> 00:18:29.155
<i>I mean. I'd lived my entire life for her.
and in that moment. I just…</i>

340
00:18:29.156 --> 00:18:31.867
<i>I hated everything about her.
So. I just… I ran.</i>

341
00:18:34.203 --> 00:18:37.205
Would've been nice if you'd had that
little epiphany before you fucked me over.

342
00:18:37.206 --> 00:18:38.332
No shit.

343
00:18:42.545 --> 00:18:44.713
- Could've come back for me. you know.
- I did come back.

344
00:18:54.682 --> 00:18:56.892
<i>I just… I couldn't get to you.
I was too late.</i>

345
00:18:57.852 --> 00:18:59.769
[Lucky] <i>So you just kept going.</i>

346
00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:00.896
[Cary] God.

347
00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:04.732
<i>There was nothing I could do.</i>

348
00:19:04.733 --> 00:19:07.736
<i>Okay. I knew you'd get out.
but I had to do something with the money.</i>

349
00:19:50.863 --> 00:19:52.573
Thank you.

350
00:20:21.936 --> 00:20:24.604
[Lucky] <i>So. what did you think
was gonna happen to me?</i>

351
00:20:24.605 --> 00:20:26.439
- I told you…
- Yeah. yeah. yeah. yeah. I know.

352
00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:28.817
I would "get out." Great. But after that?

353
00:20:28.818 --> 00:20:31.444
Like. what did you think your mother
was going to do to me?

354
00:20:31.445 --> 00:20:33.613
I thought she would come after me.

355
00:20:33.614 --> 00:20:35.824
She knew I had the money.
so I figured you'd be safe...

356
00:20:35.825 --> 00:20:38.076
She put me in a fucking trunk. Cary.

357
00:20:38.077 --> 00:20:39.202
- Fuck.
- Yes.

358
00:20:39.203 --> 00:20:40.662
She thought we were in it together.

359
00:20:40.663 --> 00:20:43.331
She was gonna have her men take me apart
to find out where you were.

360
00:20:43.332 --> 00:20:45.875
Okay. I swear to God… I swear to God.

361
00:20:45.876 --> 00:20:47.377
I didn't think she would come after you.

362
00:20:47.378 --> 00:20:49.546
Well. yeah. I guess she didn't think
you'd betray me either.

363
00:20:49.547 --> 00:20:52.632
I should've realized. I just didn't have
enough time to think it through.

364
00:20:52.633 --> 00:20:56.094
That's where I fucked up. She knew
you were the one that put her away.

365
00:20:56.095 --> 00:20:57.887
so of course she was gonna come after you.

366
00:20:57.888 --> 00:20:59.931
That's my fault.
Let's try to figure out why.

367
00:20:59.932 --> 00:21:02.226
Why'd you do it?
Why'd you work with the feds?

368
00:21:03.644 --> 00:21:05.520
Because I couldn't find another way
to protect us.

369
00:21:05.521 --> 00:21:07.522
So you just decided all our fates?

370
00:21:07.523 --> 00:21:09.482
No. I did what I had to do.

371
00:21:09.483 --> 00:21:11.860
Maybe Rand manipulated you.
Did you ever consider that?

372
00:21:11.861 --> 00:21:13.319
- No.
- Why the hell not?

373
00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:15.572
- Because I did not do it for Rand.
- Why'd you...

374
00:21:15.573 --> 00:21:17.907
I did it for my father.
and I did it for you.

375
00:21:17.908 --> 00:21:20.785
and you did what you did
for ten million dollars.

376
00:21:20.786 --> 00:21:24.747
It was never about the money.
It was never about the money. Okay?

377
00:21:24.748 --> 00:21:26.125
It was about you.

378
00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:27.793
I love you.

379
00:21:28.377 --> 00:21:30.712
- I know you still love me.
- No. I don't.

380
00:21:30.713 --> 00:21:32.297
I don't believe you.
It's not a fucking choice.

381
00:21:32.298 --> 00:21:33.965
Well. I don't care what you believe.

382
00:21:33.966 --> 00:21:35.842
Don't say you don't love me.
I know when you're lying.

383
00:21:35.843 --> 00:21:38.595
You know what? I am done
having this conversation with you.

384
00:21:38.596 --> 00:21:39.805
Give me the seed phrase.

385
00:21:40.848 --> 00:21:42.558
- No.
- No?

386
00:21:43.184 --> 00:21:46.144
No. I digitized the money so no one could
get their hands on it. including you.

387
00:21:46.145 --> 00:21:48.938
- It's not yours.
- And it's not yours either.

388
00:21:48.939 --> 00:21:50.148
And it's definitely not John's.

389
00:21:50.149 --> 00:21:52.818
I didn't go through all this bullshit
just to give it to him.

390
00:21:54.862 --> 00:21:57.364
Give it to me now.

391
00:21:59.325 --> 00:22:00.909
You won't shoot me.

392
00:22:00.910 --> 00:22:04.204
You drugged me. robbed me.
left me for dead.

393
00:22:04.205 --> 00:22:06.998
and you have no fucking idea
what I've been through since then.

394
00:22:06.999 --> 00:22:08.958
So you'll just have to
take my word for it when I say

395
00:22:08.959 --> 00:22:12.296
that I will absolutely shoot you.

396
00:22:12.797 --> 00:22:15.215
The problem with that
is the seed phrase is in here.

397
00:22:15.216 --> 00:22:16.925
so if you shoot me it dies with me.

398
00:22:16.926 --> 00:22:19.095
Well. who said anything about killing you?

399
00:22:21.722 --> 00:22:23.015
I dare you.

400
00:22:23.641 --> 00:22:25.642
[pounding on door]

401
00:22:25.643 --> 00:22:27.435
[Rand. on bullhorn]
Cary Masterson. it's the FBI.

402
00:22:27.436 --> 00:22:28.812
We know you're in there.

403
00:22:28.813 --> 00:22:32.023
Come out slowly
with your hands in the air.

404
00:22:32.024 --> 00:22:34.526
I'm gonna reach in my pocket.
Don't do anything crazy.

405
00:22:34.527 --> 00:22:36.653
- [pounds on door]
- [Rand] I don't want anybody to get hurt.

406
00:22:36.654 --> 00:22:37.862
Don't make us come in there.

407
00:22:37.863 --> 00:22:39.281
You were always a better driver.

408
00:22:44.787 --> 00:22:46.205
We're going in.

409
00:22:49.834 --> 00:22:52.419
[agent] Living room. clear.
Kitchen. clear.

410
00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:55.548
First floor. clear.

411
00:22:59.009 --> 00:23:00.010
[Rand] What the hell?

412
00:23:04.890 --> 00:23:05.891
What the hell?

413
00:23:11.981 --> 00:23:14.691
Blue Bronco! Blue Bronco! Go. go. go!

414
00:23:14.692 --> 00:23:16.735
- [agent] Let's move.
- It's Lucky.

415
00:23:17.319 --> 00:23:18.486
It's fucking Lucky.

416
00:23:18.487 --> 00:23:19.946
Put every unit on them.

417
00:23:19.947 --> 00:23:21.197
Block the freeways.

418
00:23:21.198 --> 00:23:23.367
Don't let your eyes
in the sky give them an inch!

419
00:23:24.034 --> 00:23:26.620
- [sirens blaring]
- [tires screech]

420
00:23:34.211 --> 00:23:35.879
[Cary grunts]

421
00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:38.047
For a second. I thought you were
actually gonna shoot me.

422
00:23:38.048 --> 00:23:39.341
Yeah. I still might.

423
00:23:43.179 --> 00:23:45.096
- [Cary] Car. Car.
- [Lucky speaks indistinctly]

424
00:23:45.097 --> 00:23:46.432
Yes. I have eyes!

425
00:23:48.392 --> 00:23:51.312
- Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.
- Shit. Shit. shit. shit. shit. shit.

426
00:23:52.104 --> 00:23:54.063
- We're on the opposite side of the road…
- I know that.

427
00:23:54.064 --> 00:23:55.273
…Lucky. come on.

428
00:23:55.274 --> 00:23:57.401
[helicopter whirring]

429
00:23:58.527 --> 00:23:59.611
What?

430
00:23:59.612 --> 00:24:00.905
- Turning left.
- Oh. shit. [grunts]

431
00:24:07.203 --> 00:24:09.871
[dispatcher] <i>High rate of speed.
Medium traffic growing dense.</i>

432
00:24:09.872 --> 00:24:11.372
<i>Approaching La Jolla Village Drive.</i>

433
00:24:11.373 --> 00:24:13.542
- Where is she headed?
- Shit.

434
00:24:15.002 --> 00:24:17.253
Roberts. send four black and whites

435
00:24:17.254 --> 00:24:18.963
- to the Mexican border.
- [Roberts] <i>On it.</i>

436
00:24:18.964 --> 00:24:21.299
You think she'd really try to
cross the border with this much heat?

437
00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:22.760
I don't wanna find out the hard way.

438
00:24:33.145 --> 00:24:35.688
[dispatcher] <i>Traffic is growing dense.
suspects will be blocked in.</i>

439
00:24:35.689 --> 00:24:37.274
Let's go. They've got no way out.

440
00:24:38.025 --> 00:24:40.360
All right. we need to get off this road
and head south towards Mexico.

441
00:24:40.361 --> 00:24:42.320
We? I'm not going anywhere with you.

442
00:24:42.321 --> 00:24:44.572
Okay. Well. right now
that's really not an option.

443
00:24:44.573 --> 00:24:46.366
[exclaims]
Fuck! You're gonna get us killed.

444
00:24:46.367 --> 00:24:48.535
Do you wanna get out?
I can drop you off right here.

445
00:24:48.536 --> 00:24:51.704
[Cary] I'm not asking you to forgive me.
but right now we both want the same thing.

446
00:24:51.705 --> 00:24:53.706
I just need you to trust me
for about ten minutes. okay?

447
00:24:53.707 --> 00:24:56.209
Well. we can't go anywhere
until we lose this helicopter.

448
00:24:56.210 --> 00:24:58.336
[Cary] Yeah. and how the hell
are we gonna do that?

449
00:24:58.337 --> 00:25:00.755
- How the hell are we gonna do that?
- I'm thinking.

450
00:25:00.756 --> 00:25:02.925
- Well. what are you thinking. Lucky?
- Just trust me.

451
00:25:19.108 --> 00:25:21.276
[dispatcher 2] <i>Air One to ground.
we pulled the wrong vehicle</i>

452
00:25:21.277 --> 00:25:22.360
<i>from under the overpass.</i>

453
00:25:22.361 --> 00:25:24.404
<i>Negative visual on the blue Bronco.</i>

454
00:25:24.405 --> 00:25:26.073
<i>Repeat. we lost visual.</i>

455
00:25:29.952 --> 00:25:30.994
[agent] Move in.

456
00:25:30.995 --> 00:25:32.538
Passenger's side. check.

457
00:25:33.414 --> 00:25:34.415
It's clear.

458
00:25:38.711 --> 00:25:39.920
All right. where we going?

459
00:25:40.546 --> 00:25:41.797
Somewhere we can blend in.

460
00:25:46.302 --> 00:25:47.595
Roberts.

461
00:25:49.805 --> 00:25:51.014
What the hell happened?

462
00:25:51.015 --> 00:25:53.350
- [Roberts] They ditched the car.
- [Gates] No shit.

463
00:25:59.565 --> 00:26:01.567
[radio chatter]

464
00:26:13.871 --> 00:26:15.039
They're up there.

465
00:26:15.581 --> 00:26:17.123
They're up there on foot.

466
00:26:17.124 --> 00:26:19.793
I want every cop car
to circle topside and corral them.

467
00:26:19.794 --> 00:26:21.294
- The suspects are on foot.
- They're not far.

468
00:26:21.295 --> 00:26:22.546
Form a perimeter. Let's go!

469
00:26:23.923 --> 00:26:25.256
Can I ask you something?

470
00:26:25.257 --> 00:26:26.966
[sighs] Now's not really a good time.

471
00:26:26.967 --> 00:26:29.929
John asked you to take the money for him.
Why'd you do it?

472
00:26:31.555 --> 00:26:34.224
Our parents were locked up.
we had the life you always wanted.

473
00:26:34.225 --> 00:26:36.893
you were happy. and then John calls
and you just give it all up for him?

474
00:26:36.894 --> 00:26:39.021
- Well. they would've come for us anyway.
- Who?

475
00:26:39.647 --> 00:26:41.564
Whittaker. Your mother.

476
00:26:41.565 --> 00:26:43.233
They either would've thought
that I had something to do with it

477
00:26:43.234 --> 00:26:44.901
or they would've used me
to get John to talk.

478
00:26:44.902 --> 00:26:46.069
Either way. that life was over.

479
00:26:46.070 --> 00:26:47.570
- Yeah. you wanna know what I think?
- Not really.

480
00:26:47.571 --> 00:26:49.907
I think you don't know
how to say no to your dad.

481
00:26:51.242 --> 00:26:52.660
[tires squeal]

482
00:26:53.285 --> 00:26:54.787
You're together?

483
00:26:55.371 --> 00:26:58.332
- [Lucky breathing heavily]
- Well. get in. We don't have time.

484
00:26:59.291 --> 00:27:00.417
Honey. I can forgive you.

485
00:27:01.752 --> 00:27:03.170
Just get in!

486
00:27:04.463 --> 00:27:06.215
[sighs] Idiot.

487
00:27:08.509 --> 00:27:10.094
- [pedestrian yelps]
- [person] Hey!

488
00:27:10.761 --> 00:27:11.762
[panting]

489
00:27:12.596 --> 00:27:14.473
- [grunting]
- [person] Asshole!

490
00:27:19.645 --> 00:27:21.855
Excuse me! Please. you need to help me.

491
00:27:21.856 --> 00:27:23.523
You see that man. he is chasing me.

492
00:27:23.524 --> 00:27:24.607
I do not feel safe.

493
00:27:24.608 --> 00:27:26.317
Please. I don't feel safe with him...

494
00:27:26.318 --> 00:27:27.652
Just leave me alone.

495
00:27:27.653 --> 00:27:28.862
[Lucky] Sir. I'm not safe.

496
00:27:28.863 --> 00:27:31.782
[panting] Fuck was that?

497
00:27:34.702 --> 00:27:36.202
[engine starts]

498
00:27:36.203 --> 00:27:37.496
[engine revs]

499
00:27:41.500 --> 00:27:42.834
[Gates] They've gotta be here.

500
00:27:42.835 --> 00:27:44.461
If they're still on foot.

501
00:27:44.462 --> 00:27:45.795
She could've lifted a car.

502
00:27:45.796 --> 00:27:48.883
If that's the case. then we have no idea
what the fuck we're looking for.

503
00:27:50.468 --> 00:27:51.885
We go inland.

504
00:27:51.886 --> 00:27:53.511
There's a million different routes
that we can take there

505
00:27:53.512 --> 00:27:55.180
and we'll just disappear.

506
00:27:55.181 --> 00:27:57.725
You sure you don't wanna head south
and just wait at the border?

507
00:27:58.392 --> 00:27:59.642
- Wait at the…
- Yes.

508
00:27:59.643 --> 00:28:01.436
That's exactly
what they're expecting us to do.

509
00:28:01.437 --> 00:28:03.313
I just think it's our quickest out. Lucky.

510
00:28:03.314 --> 00:28:04.565
- Wait. what are you...
- Lucky.

511
00:28:15.493 --> 00:28:16.827
- They looking?
- I don't know.

512
00:28:18.245 --> 00:28:20.164
But don't look.

513
00:28:23.375 --> 00:28:25.461
I said don't look. Cary.

514
00:28:29.507 --> 00:28:30.508
Careful.

515
00:28:42.103 --> 00:28:43.312
[sighs]

516
00:28:47.108 --> 00:28:48.691
Okay. A million routes.

517
00:28:48.692 --> 00:28:50.653
I don't know what that means.
We need to pick one.

518
00:28:51.487 --> 00:28:54.239
I am clearly driving right now.
Can you just navigate for me. please?

519
00:28:54.240 --> 00:28:56.449
- If you drive. we'll be driving all day.
- Fuck!

520
00:28:56.450 --> 00:28:58.118
Oh. Jesus.

521
00:28:58.119 --> 00:28:59.703
- [grunts]
- [Priscilla] That was them.

522
00:29:04.959 --> 00:29:06.751
Okay. okay. okay. okay.

523
00:29:06.752 --> 00:29:07.878
I'm just gonna do it.

524
00:29:09.088 --> 00:29:11.173
- Shit. Shit. shit. shit. shit. shit.
- Whoa. Whoa.

525
00:29:13.050 --> 00:29:15.344
- Fuck! No!
- Shit.

526
00:29:15.970 --> 00:29:17.513
Get… Stay on them. Stay on them.

527
00:29:21.559 --> 00:29:23.769
- Faster. Lucky. Come on!
- I'm trying. please. just…

528
00:29:26.397 --> 00:29:28.023
- [Cary exclaims]
- [tires screech]

529
00:29:36.574 --> 00:29:38.033
- Shit.
- [car horn honks]

530
00:29:46.792 --> 00:29:47.918
Okay.

531
00:29:48.794 --> 00:29:51.422
[sirens wailing]

532
00:29:57.678 --> 00:29:58.804
Catch them on the other side.

533
00:30:02.808 --> 00:30:04.393
Ah. we're fucked. We're fucked.

534
00:30:06.061 --> 00:30:07.980
- Lucky. stop.
- Stop.

535
00:30:15.196 --> 00:30:16.655
Holy shit!

536
00:30:17.490 --> 00:30:18.783
This is crazy.

537
00:30:46.852 --> 00:30:48.229
- Cary?
- I know.

538
00:30:49.897 --> 00:30:50.980
I don't regret us.

539
00:30:50.981 --> 00:30:52.233
Neither do I.

540
00:30:58.239 --> 00:30:59.322
What are you doing?

541
00:30:59.323 --> 00:31:00.825
Buying us some time.

542
00:31:01.492 --> 00:31:02.827
Shit.

543
00:31:06.288 --> 00:31:07.706
Fuck!

544
00:31:21.637 --> 00:31:22.847
[grunts]

545
00:31:27.017 --> 00:31:28.310
Cary?

546
00:31:29.145 --> 00:31:30.146
[yelps]

547
00:31:31.981 --> 00:31:33.732
[both grunting]

548
00:31:51.292 --> 00:31:54.837
[no audible dialogue]

549
00:32:22.698 --> 00:32:25.242
- It's over. Lucky.
- [panting]

550
00:32:28.996 --> 00:32:30.414
Where's he going?

551
00:32:32.583 --> 00:32:33.918
[Lucky panting]

552
00:32:35.336 --> 00:32:36.754
Couldn't keep him out of it.

553
00:32:37.963 --> 00:32:39.548
What? Wh… [pants]

554
00:32:40.424 --> 00:32:42.258
- I'm sorry.
- No. wait. What are you talking about?

555
00:32:42.259 --> 00:32:44.636
He was in deeper than I realized
and it was out of my hands.

556
00:32:44.637 --> 00:32:46.888
No. no. no. You… You promised me.

557
00:32:46.889 --> 00:32:48.056
I did what I could.

558
00:32:48.057 --> 00:32:49.808
- [stammers] Sorry?
- I'm sorry.

559
00:32:49.809 --> 00:32:51.851
No. You can't just do that.

560
00:32:51.852 --> 00:32:53.478
It was out of your hands?

561
00:32:53.479 --> 00:32:55.230
You used me!

562
00:32:55.231 --> 00:32:57.107
- I'm sorry. Let's go.
- No.

563
00:32:57.108 --> 00:33:00.193
Okay. wait. No. no. no.
You… you… you can't do that.

564
00:33:00.194 --> 00:33:01.945
Okay? We had a deal.

565
00:33:01.946 --> 00:33:04.614
You promised me! I helped you!

566
00:33:04.615 --> 00:33:07.784
Do you understand that this is my life?

567
00:33:07.785 --> 00:33:10.078
What is wrong with you? You are a liar!

568
00:33:10.079 --> 00:33:12.581
[sobs] You lied to me!

569
00:33:13.165 --> 00:33:19.004
[screaming. crying]

570
00:33:26.637 --> 00:33:28.556
- [breathes heavily]
- [groans] They shot me.

571
00:33:29.598 --> 00:33:32.475
- [coughs]
- Cary! [breathes heavily]

572
00:33:32.476 --> 00:33:34.811
- [grunting]
- Oh. Cary. Cary. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

573
00:33:34.812 --> 00:33:37.439
I'm sorry. sorry. sorry. Hey. baby-baby.
Don't look down. Don't look down.

574
00:33:37.440 --> 00:33:39.441
- Hey. look at me. Look at me.
- [grunts]

575
00:33:39.442 --> 00:33:42.193
- Hey. Hey. it's okay. It's okay.
- [grunting]

576
00:33:42.194 --> 00:33:43.570
Goddamn it.

577
00:33:43.571 --> 00:33:46.114
It's okay.
It's-It's-It's-It's gonna be fine.

578
00:33:46.115 --> 00:33:48.283
I think the gun was a bad choice.

579
00:33:48.284 --> 00:33:51.161
- Hey. Hey. honey. Don't look at it.
- [panting]

580
00:33:51.162 --> 00:33:52.871
Look at me. Hey. focus.

581
00:33:52.872 --> 00:33:54.706
- Cary. I need you to focus.
- Yeah.

582
00:33:54.707 --> 00:33:58.752
I need you to focus. Look at me.
Look at me. Breathe. baby. Breathe.

583
00:33:59.378 --> 00:34:01.963
Yeah. there we go. There we go. honey.

584
00:34:01.964 --> 00:34:05.467
It's gonna be fine. It's gonna be fine.
It's gonna be fine.

585
00:34:05.468 --> 00:34:06.718
I think I'm gonna die.

586
00:34:06.719 --> 00:34:09.929
No. honey. No. No. baby.

587
00:34:10.681 --> 00:34:13.141
It's okay. It's okay.

588
00:34:13.893 --> 00:34:15.853
Hey. Hey.

589
00:34:18.230 --> 00:34:21.691
Cary? Cary?

590
00:34:21.692 --> 00:34:24.820
[breathes heavily]

591
00:34:25.529 --> 00:34:28.657
You… You were happy.

592
00:34:29.407 --> 00:34:30.576
You were happy…

593
00:34:34.996 --> 00:34:35.998
Cary?

594
00:34:37.750 --> 00:34:39.293
Cary. open your eyes. Look at me.

595
00:34:40.711 --> 00:34:43.005
Look at me. Cary! You can't leave me!

596
00:34:44.255 --> 00:34:45.257
Cary!

597
00:34:46.717 --> 00:34:49.804
Fucking wake up! You can't leave me.

598
00:34:52.889 --> 00:34:56.225
[crying]

599
00:34:56.226 --> 00:34:57.561
No!

600
00:34:58.771 --> 00:35:00.940
[crying] Fucking wake up!

601
00:35:02.233 --> 00:35:03.859
Come on!

602
00:35:06.612 --> 00:35:08.405
[sniffs] Please.

603
00:35:11.492 --> 00:35:15.496
[crying]

604
00:35:19.125 --> 00:35:21.127
[crying]

605
00:35:31.971 --> 00:35:34.181
[approaching sirens]

606
00:35:38.144 --> 00:35:39.145
[grunts]

607
00:35:41.981 --> 00:35:45.484
- Wait.
- [Rand grunting. panting]

608
00:35:55.035 --> 00:35:56.245
[Gates] Rand. wait!

609
00:36:08.132 --> 00:36:09.884
[breathes shakily]

610
00:36:14.430 --> 00:36:17.307
[panting]

611
00:36:17.308 --> 00:36:19.351
- [Gates] Where did she go?
- [sirens wailing]

612
00:36:23.856 --> 00:36:25.023
Rand!

613
00:36:25.024 --> 00:36:26.691
- [Rand thuds]
- Officer down!

614
00:36:26.692 --> 00:36:28.527
Rand! Hey.

615
00:37:06.816 --> 00:37:08.526
[panting]

616
00:37:14.448 --> 00:37:15.491
No!

617
00:37:15.991 --> 00:37:19.369
No! My baby!

618
00:37:19.370 --> 00:37:22.789
- No. you can't. You can't. Come on.
- No! Let me go. Let me go.

619
00:37:22.790 --> 00:37:26.292
[sobbing] No! No!

620
00:37:26.293 --> 00:37:30.131
No! No!

621
00:37:31.424 --> 00:37:33.008
[wails]

622
00:37:35.886 --> 00:37:38.055
[screams]

623
00:37:38.806 --> 00:37:40.433
My baby!

624
00:38:06.083 --> 00:38:08.335
["Into the Black" playing]

624
00:38:09.305 --> 00:39:09.360
